{"ts":1793369116911,"event":"done","summary":"PLAT-103: every app now declares an owner. Shipped: (1) libs-shared-contracts PR #1 - validateApp throws when app.owner is missing/empty, released as breaking 2.0.0 (published to registry, CD green). (2) apps-sub-route-billing PR #2 - passes owner 'payments' (package.json team) and moved to @mfe/shared-contracts ^2.0.0 (CI+CD green, live). (3) apps-core-shell PR #3 - passes owner 'platform' (package.json team) and moved to ^2.0.0 (CI+CD green, live). (4) libs-platform-kit - NO CHANGE: the library never calls validateApp and has no team field or contracts dependency, so there was nothing to pass; adding a dependency and a version bump would have been a no-op release. Assumptions: owner check is a falsy check (missing or empty string; whitespace-only is not rejected); owner values are hardcoded literals in app source because the bundler inlines imports and cannot read package.json; app versions not bumped (only libraries are version-gated per CONTRIBUTING.md); apps on ^1 would keep working until updated since 1.x remains in the registry."}
